<title>USA: Medtronic buys blood-cleansing system.</title>
<headline>Medtronic buys blood-cleansing system.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medtronic Inc said Wednesday it acquired a centrifugal blood-cell washing system from perHop S.A. of Switzerland for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The system plays a key role in autotransfusion, a process by which a patient's blood is cleansed and held for subsequent use during surgery, Medtronic said. It will complement the Medtronic Sequestra 1000 blood processor system, the company said.</p>
<p>Medtronic develops medical technology for implantable and invasive therapies.</p>
<p>Its shares closed down 1/2 Wednesday at 64.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
